    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@value": "CPTP is list of optional headings for correlations, and some are not applicable for all soil types.\nThe CPTP group is to be used to transfer derived soil parameters determined from CPT test data. The requirement for this information as part of ground investigation reporting shall be fully specified at the outset of the investigation. The specification may need to detail the interpretative method(s) to be used.\nDetails of the standards and methods used to carry out calculations shall be included in CPTM group.\nWhere soil type interpretation leading to borehole style stratum descriptions is carried out the information should be entered in GEOL.\nThe coefficient of consolidation is calculated from dissipation testing data which is included in CPDG and CPDT.",
        "@language": "en"
      }
    ],
